E1 found that no PyTorch-only candidate matches Tb. Tb is flat at about 1.22× the time of a plain cuBLAS matmul with no residual add. So a GEMM with the residual fused for free would sit at about Tb. r0's fused call is 7–15% slower than plain matmul, so the lever is H10. The candidate is r0 resubmitted unchanged. I re-ran it and it passed 16/16.

